    "notes": "<p><i>When a sentient being dies alone in space, their spirit sometimes connects to the void.</i></p><p><strong>Movement:</strong> NEAR (fly)</p>",
    "description": "<p><strong>Attacks:</strong> 2 entropic touch +5 (1d8 + energy drain) or drift</p><p>Greater</p><p><strong>Undead.</strong> Immune to morale checks. Only damaged by silver or magical sources.</p><p><strong>Incorporeal.</strong> In place of attacks, become corporeal or incorporeal.</p><p>Energy</p><p><strong>Drain.</strong> 1d4 CON damage or drain one</p><p>Energy</p><p><strong>Cell.</strong> Death if reduced to 0 CON.</p><p><strong>Drift.</strong> Must be corporeal. One target, CLOSE range. Contested CHA check. If ghost wins, it forces the target's spirit from their body for 2d4 rounds. The body is unconscious in this state. If the body is killed while the spirit is drifting, the spirit becomes a void ghost.</p>",
